<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Magan</h1><p class="st-meta">2300 BCE – 550 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The copper land of south-eastern Arabia, known to Mesopotamian kings as the source of metal and hard stone shipped up the Gulf.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Magan appears in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuneiform">cuneiform</a> texts from the 23rd century BCE, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad">Sargon of Akkad</a> recorded that ships from Magan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meluhha">Meluhha</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dilmun">Dilmun</a> moored at his capital. The name covered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>-bearing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hajar-mountains">Hajar Mountains</a> of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates</a>, home of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umm-an-nar-culture">Umm an-Nar culture</a> with its round stone tombs and towers such as those at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hili-archaeological-park">Hili</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bat-al-khutm-and-al-ayn">Bat</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of its politics. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naram-sin">Naram-Sin</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a> claimed to have defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manium">Manium</a>, lord of Magan, and brought back diorite for statues. Magan exported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>, diorite and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">timber</a> in Magan-boats, and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-dynasty-of-ur">Ur III</a> texts record merchants trading wool, textiles and oil for its copper. Whether it was ever a single kingdom or a federation of oasis communities is unclear.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>References fade after the early 2nd millennium BCE as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dilmun">Dilmun</a> took over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> trade. The name revived in Assyrian records and as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maka-satrapy">Maka</a>, a land listed among the subjects of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> in the 6th century BCE. Its copper mines and tombs remain the main witnesses to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 2300 BCE – 550 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Arabia and the Gulf</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:13.93%;width:34.83%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>2300 BCE – 550 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/24th-century-bce">24th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Manium</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/oman">Oman</a>, <a href="/countries/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Makkan</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1425&amp;focus=magan" aria-label="Magan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6216 1361 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Magan lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6129 1232h0M6092 1134h0"/><pat